# Header: Two virtiofs (caller_owner) improvements for macOS bind mounts:
#
# 1. Explicit chown tracking (#382): Apple's Virtualization.framework virtiofs
#    server accepts FUSE_SETATTR(FATTR_UID | FATTR_GID) and returns 0 without
#    storing uid/gid, so chown appeared to succeed while leaving files owned by
#    the caller (root -> 0:0) and blocking subsequent chmod by the new owner.
#    Record explicit chown/lchown/fchown ownership in memory on struct
#    fuse_inode (chown_uid/chown_gid + FUSE_I_CHOWN_UID/GID), strip
#    FATTR_UID/FATTR_GID before sending FUSE_SETATTR (skipping the request when
#    no other attributes remain), return the recorded uid/gid from stat and
#    attribute refreshes, and enforce standard owner/group/other mode bits and
#    setattr ownership checks against it (falling back to caller_owner from
#    0008 for unchowned inodes).
#
# 2. Close-to-open page/dir caching and round-trip reduction (#415): Apple's
#    virtiofs server returns open_flags = 0 (no FOPEN_KEEP_CACHE, no
#    FOPEN_CACHE_DIR, no FOPEN_NOFLUSH) and leaves FUSE_AUTO_INVAL_DATA off,
#    causing every warm open to evict the inode's page cache and re-read from
#    the host, every warm readdir to re-issue READDIRPLUS/READDIR, every read
#    to invalidate STATX_ATIME on noatime mounts (forcing redundant GETATTR),
#    every read-only close to send a no-op FUSE_FLUSH, and every close to block
#    synchronously on FUSE_RELEASE even without submounts. Enable
#    auto_inval_data, FOPEN_KEEP_CACHE, and FOPEN_CACHE_DIR with close-to-open
#    FUSE_GETATTR revalidation on warm opens (plus page-cache invalidation on
#    /proc/kiri-fsnotify M events) so host edits remain immediately visible
#    while unchanged warm reads hit the guest page and directory caches. Skip
#    no-op FUSE_FLUSH on read-only opens when no_lock and !writeback_cache,
#    skip STATX_ATIME invalidation on caller_owner mounts, and send FUSE_RELEASE
#    asynchronously when no submounts are mounted.
